{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matrixorigin/matrixone/pulls/29837","id":4813380168,"node_id":"PR_kwDOFEPiGM8AAAABHuZaSA","html_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/29837","diff_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/29837.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/matrixorigin/matrixone/pull/29837.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/matrixorigin/matrixone/issues/29837","number":29837,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"fix(sql): avoid lifecycle convoy for scalar RC truncate","user":{"login":"XuPeng-SH","id":39627130,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5NjI3MTMw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/39627130?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH","html_url":"https://github.com/XuPeng-SH","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/XuPeng-SH/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What type of PR is this?\n\n- [ ] API-change\n- [x] BUG\n- [x] Improvement\n- [ ] Documentation\n- [ ] Feature\n- [x] Test and CI\n- [ ] Code Refactoring\n\n## Which issue(s) this PR fixes:\n\nAddresses #29400: fresh RC TRUNCATE should wait on first lifecycle contention, and an independent ordinary scalar TRUNCATE should finish while DROP waits for another transaction's DML. Historical convoy limits remain, so this PR does not close the whole issue.\n\n## What this PR does / why we need it:\n\nThe broad global lifecycle gate lets a waiting DROP stall unrelated TRUNCATE. For permanent ordinary tables under pessimistic RC, certify that there are no FK relationships, secondary indexes, partitions, history owners or branch components; reuse existing C/G/D/K/catalog/storage locks and the applied frontier, then run the existing replacement executor under G S. Check tenant-owned user snapshots and SYS history using physical and stable logical identity. Every excluded shape, optimized DELETE, SI and temporary tables retain existing broad behavior.\n\nFK CREATE/publication/forward-reference repair acquires actual G X before effects using existing typed plan fields. Validate planned parent generations at CREATE and ADD FK's existing locking seam. The outer destructive storage lock also owns the definition-change commit fence, which lets stale physical-generation lock callers rebuild instead of silently refreshing. Parent validation follows the planner’s parallel named FK fields without an unused unnamed-parent fallback. Extend the synchronous nested DROP receipt to one certified operator/account/table generation; broad nested CREATE borrows its outer G X without re-admission. No new persistent state, cache, protobuf field or replacement executor is introduced.\n\nFresh G acquisition waits with existing cancellation/deadlines; retained promotion remains FastFail and preserves whole-transaction rollback. The scoped path adds bounded metadata reads and frontier validation for independent progress; no throughput improvement is claimed. FK CREATE/repair deliberately retains broad serialization. Deployment assumes maintenance cutover with drained old transactions.\n\nValidation on the rebased code (main `dd38098853`), Linux/amd64, Go 1.27.1 and stamped native libraries:\n\n- Owning compile package normal and complete `-race`: passed.\n- Existing authenticated two-CN root normal and `-race`: passed, including scalar/indexed retired-definition fences, parent replacement/deletion while FK CREATE waits, and snapshot/FK publication after negative preflight. All scenarios reuse one fixture.\n- Existing FK branch clone compatibility regression: passed on the rebased implementation.\n- Public fault injection after successful nested DROP: passed on the rebased production code; CREATE failure restores the original physical ID and row, and a subsequent TRUNCATE succeeds. This diagnostic overlay remains outside the PR.\n- Exact-root bounded race stress: passed (`B=30s`, measured `T=35.13s`, `count=1`).\n- Fresh normal coverage profiles parsed with the CI script and complete PR diff: **143/189 = 75.66%**, passing the strict >75% gate without changing policy.\n- `go vet` and configured incremental golangci-lint: passed, zero introduced issues. Repository molint reports seven recover diagnostics in five files byte-identical to the rebased main.\n\nCorrective design and final overall review use actual `gpt-6.1-sol` / `xhigh` CLI, verified from rollout metadata, session `01a12710-062c-7840-86a8-c66927427fd1`. Both design and final overall review passed with no unresolved material blocker. Current complete reviewed 12-file patch SHA256: `cb0ec82161e87fc23becc3c7d1049d8822449b9fb172ae9e49c28e86afecfb45`.\n\nQA also identified an existing tenant historical-lineage retention defect: broad positive history probes and compaction read SYS snapshots only. The new scalar path excludes those historical tables; their existing retention implementation is unchanged and is not claimed fixed here. Reproduction evidence is retained separately. The additional definition-change correction adds no lock acquisition or query. New remote CI is pending; the coverage result above is local current-code validation.\n\n","created_at":"2026-10-10T18:10:51Z","updated_at":"2026-10-11T01:36:04Z","closed_at":"2026-10-11T01:36:02Z","merged_at":"2026-10-11T01:36:01Z","merge_commit_sha":"4022729da24d71b082c22b52aaed3faba2b77ea5","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[{"login":"fengttt","id":